(5604303, 810926, 80096, '<td valign="top">Very nice, Scott!!!</td>', 'Very nice, Scott!!!', '2009-08-08 20:37:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5604322, 809931, 87808, '<td valign="top">HI from teh CC CLub, <br/> <br/>I think what this shot is sufferening from is a bright background that overtakes teh forgreound. A closer crop on teh left may have helped a little as well. This could definitely do with some contrast and or exposure sliding. He has such a happy face and that needs to be brought out, you have so many details that could be brought out with a little dodge and burn, some tweak in selective colour, shadow highlights. <br/> <br/>play around with it and see what you come up with!</td>', 'HI from teh CC CLub,  I think what this shot is sufferening from is a bright background that overtakes teh forgreound. A closer crop on teh left may have helped a little as well. This could definitely do with some contrast and or exposure sliding. He has such a happy face and that needs to be brought out, you have so many details that could be brought out with a little dodge and burn, some tweak in selective colour, shadow highlights.  play around with it and see what you come up with!', '2009-08-08 21:13:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5604337, 808439, 31637, '<td valign="top">I voted this a 7, I was completely enthralled by the streaky rain, captured so well against the bundle of flowers.</td>', 'I voted this a 7, I was completely enthralled by the streaky rain, captured so well against the bundle of flowers.', '2009-08-08 21:33:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5604348, 809489, 39850, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg"/> <br/> <br/><u>Critique Club Critique</u> <br/> <br/><b>First Impressions</b> <br/>The light <i>is</i> nice.  A bit of a snapshot feel to the image, however the quality and lighting pull it beyond that ''realm''.  I gave this a 4 during voting.<br/> <br/><b>Photograph Information, Technicals &amp; Composition Review</b> <br/>Photographic technicals all look to have worked quite well.  What would really strengthen this image is a refined crop, or, in retrospect (so as to speak), to be able to ''align'' the background behind him, especially the head area, to complement him.<br/> <br/>As is, whilst I like the vertical framing and think this does suit this, I think a tighter crop may have given this a little extra.  I did try it, but after doing so not sure, it changes the feel of the image.  I guess it depends what you were aiming for.  The shadow is interesting on the left, but it is ''chopped'', the rocks are a nice element, and I like the ''boyhoodness'' of his clothing, including his sandals.  If the quality is there, this image likely lends itself well to a head and shoulders crop, especially to really showcase that nice catch of light in his eyes.<br/> <br/><b>Comments, Score &amp; Placement Review</b> <br/>373/419 is fairly low down the pack and your score of 4.92 seems a bit harsh for the quality of the image.  My only guess (before reading the comments) is that people may not have lingered long enough to appreciate the interesting elements to the image.<br/> <br/>All your comments are helpful, one in particular extremely so.<br/> <br/><b>Summary</b> <br/>Of course a personal image, which I''m sure will be treasured, but given a similar opportunity again, just a fraction check on the surroundings and composition and, if possible without ruining ''a moment'', some encouragement or direction to allow the boy''s character to shine through a little more.</td>', '  Critique Club Critique  First Impressions The light is nice.  A bit of a snapshot feel to the image, however the quality and lighting pull it beyond that ''realm''.  I gave this a 4 during voting. Photograph Information, Technicals & Composition Review Photographic technicals all look to have worked quite well.  What would really strengthen this image is a refined crop, or, in retrospect (so as to speak), to be able to ''align'' the background behind him, especially the head area, to complement him. As is, whilst I like the vertical framing and think this does suit this, I think a tighter crop may have given this a little extra.  I did try it, but after doing so not sure, it changes the feel of the image.  I guess it depends what you were aiming for.  The shadow is interesting on the left, but it is ''chopped'', the rocks are a nice element, and I like the ''boyhoodness'' of his clothing, including his sandals.  If the quality is there, this image likely lends itself well to a head and shoulders crop, especially to really showcase that nice catch of light in his eyes. Comments, Score & Placement Review 373/419 is fairly low down the pack and your score of 4.92 seems a bit harsh for the quality of the image.  My only guess (before reading the comments) is that people may not have lingered long enough to appreciate the interesting elements to the image. All your comments are helpful, one in particular extremely so. Summary Of course a personal image, which I''m sure will be treasured, but given a similar opportunity again, just a fraction check on the surroundings and composition and, if possible without ruining ''a moment'', some encouragement or direction to allow the boy''s character to shine through a little more.', '2009-08-08 22:06:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5604356, 804897, 39850, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg"/> <br/> <br/><u>Critique Club Critique</u> <br/> <br/><b>First Impressions</b> <br/>Oh, yes, an easy image for me to comment on.  I gave this a 7 during voted and really liked it.  First impression was, as best I recall, super strong composition and the grain really worked in this image, giving it an old world, almost 50''s feel.<br/> <br/><b>Photograph Information, Technicals &amp; Composition Review</b> <br/>Ahh, on reading your Photographer''s Comments I see the ''noise'' was deliberate.  Good call.  <br/> <br/>I really like your choice of crop and the somewhat muted colors.  My biggest nit-pick is probably the vignetting, it does add to a feel overall, but I''d like to see it a little more subtle.<br/> <br/>It is a fun shot and there is a nice harmony/balance in the fashions and facial expressions/poses.<br/> <br/><b>Comments, Score &amp; Placement Review</b> <br/>114/419, I''d guess is a good placing, considering this is likely not to many people''s taste.  Score of 6.01 is good, at least you made it over the 6 line for an unusual and unique type image, especially one that uses grain/noise as you have.<br/> <br/>Most of your commenters enjoyed the use of grain/noise.  With 13 comments and an average commenter''s vote of 8.0, that is pretty good going in itself.<br/> <br/><b>Summary</b> <br/><i>Maybe</i> a more refined crop at the top, but very minor.  As much as like the mutedness of the image, perhaps a fraction tweaking for a tiny bit more pop, which would also likely enhance the grain and give it touch more grit and ''life'', but your call of course.  A good unique image and capture of an interesting juxtaposition, well seen.</td>', '  Critique Club Critique  First Impressions Oh, yes, an easy image for me to comment on.  I gave this a 7 during voted and really liked it.  First impression was, as best I recall, super strong composition and the grain really worked in this image, giving it an old world, almost 50''s feel. Photograph Information, Technicals & Composition Review Ahh, on reading your Photographer''s Comments I see the ''noise'' was deliberate.  Good call.   I really like your choice of crop and the somewhat muted colors.  My biggest nit-pick is probably the vignetting, it does add to a feel overall, but I''d like to see it a little more subtle. It is a fun shot and there is a nice harmony/balance in the fashions and facial expressions/poses. Comments, Score & Placement Review 114/419, I''d guess is a good placing, considering this is likely not to many people''s taste.  Score of 6.01 is good, at least you made it over the 6 line for an unusual and unique type image, especially one that uses grain/noise as you have. Most of your commenters enjoyed the use of grain/noise.  With 13 comments and an average commenter''s vote of 8.0, that is pretty good going in itself. Summary Maybe a more refined crop at the top, but very minor.  As much as like the mutedness of the image, perhaps a fraction tweaking for a tiny bit more pop, which would also likely enhance the grain and give it touch more grit and ''life'', but your call of course.  A good unique image and capture of an interesting juxtaposition, well seen.', '2009-08-08 22:18:38.000000', NULL, 0),
