(5724954, 809161, 93565, '<td valign="top">Wow, you did an excellent job capturing this building. I don''t recall the robot being there when I visited, but it just adds another interesting element to things. You''ve really got some interesting colors in the building itself though.</td>', 'Wow, you did an excellent job capturing this building. I don''t recall the robot being there when I visited, but it just adds another interesting element to things. You''ve really got some interesting colors in the building itself though.', '2009-11-12 22:47:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5726032, 810654, 69008, '<td valign="top">The dark BG in this highlights the features and eye very nicely. I suspect that you may have brought this shot up from being underexposed by the look in the darker areas of the feathers.  It''s a lovely shot, and the bit of noise gives it that "film shot" effect.  Grays are noisy so it fits. Grays are the most wonderful of birds when they are in their "sweet bird" mode.</td>', 'The dark BG in this highlights the features and eye very nicely. I suspect that you may have brought this shot up from being underexposed by the look in the darker areas of the feathers.  It''s a lovely shot, and the bit of noise gives it that "film shot" effect.  Grays are noisy so it fits. Grays are the most wonderful of birds when they are in their "sweet bird" mode.', '2009-11-13 23:00:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5744449, 810640, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hi Sean. This is a typical shot of them running from danger, ears up and both looking at the source of danger or the lead Zebra. In the African dry season as you know when you took this shot (Winter months June July August or so) theres no rain and it''s dusty largely from the heard stirring it up. Commercial photography of Zebra''s tries to avoid this to make them "pop" out as Juliette mentioned.</td>', 'Hi Sean. This is a typical shot of them running from danger, ears up and both looking at the source of danger or the lead Zebra. In the African dry season as you know when you took this shot (Winter months June July August or so) theres no rain and it''s dusty largely from the heard stirring it up. Commercial photography of Zebra''s tries to avoid this to make them "pop" out as Juliette mentioned.', '2009-11-28 03:47:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5764170, 810326, 97225, '<td valign="top">What an amazing image! That lens is totally cool, and  the scene you have chosen to employ it on, certainly beautiful in its own right,  becomes spectacular. The beautiful jewel-like colours are just perfect in this context.</td>', 'What an amazing image! That lens is totally cool, and  the scene you have chosen to employ it on, certainly beautiful in its own right,  becomes spectacular. The beautiful jewel-like colours are just perfect in this context.', '2009-12-11 17:52:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5764551, 810912, 90495, '<td valign="top">Love these greens. Beautiful image Michelle.</td>', 'Love these greens. Beautiful image Michelle.', '2009-12-12 09:23:38.000000', NULL, 0),
